<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Interview Bibles on SDET Interview Preparation Kit</title><link>https://notxkcd.github.io/sdet-prep-site/qa-vault/interview-bibles/</link><description>Recent content in Interview Bibles on SDET Interview Preparation Kit</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 31 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://notxkcd.github.io/sdet-prep-site/qa-vault/interview-bibles/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Core Java Deep Dive</title><link>https://notxkcd.github.io/sdet-prep-site/qa-vault/interview-bibles/core-java-deep-dive/</link><pubDate>Sat, 31 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://notxkcd.github.io/sdet-prep-site/qa-vault/interview-bibles/core-java-deep-dive/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="1-exception-handling-mastery"&gt;1. Exception Handling Mastery&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id="checked-vs-unchecked"&gt;Checked vs Unchecked&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Checked&lt;/strong&gt;: Compiler forces you to handle (e.g., &lt;code&gt;IOException&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unchecked&lt;/strong&gt;: Runtime logic errors (e.g., &lt;code&gt;NullPointerException&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="throw-vs-throws"&gt;throw vs throws&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;throw&lt;/strong&gt;: Used inside a method to actually raise the error.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;throws&lt;/strong&gt;: Used in the method signature to warn callers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="modern-try-with-resources"&gt;Modern try-with-resources&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Automatically closes resources (files, DB connections) that implement &lt;code&gt;AutoCloseable&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#586e75;background-color:#eee8d5;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-java" data-lang="java"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#859900"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span style="color:#268bd2"&gt;BufferedReader&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#268bd2"&gt;br&lt;/span&gt; = &lt;span style="color:#859900"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#268bd2"&gt;BufferedReader&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style="color:#859900"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#268bd2"&gt;FileReader&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style="color:#2aa198"&gt;&amp;#34;config.txt&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;))) {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#93a1a1;font-style:italic"&gt;// Logic here&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;} &lt;span style="color:#859900"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span style="color:#268bd2"&gt;IOException&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#268bd2"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;) { ... }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="2-functional-programming--lambdas"&gt;2. Functional Programming &amp;amp; Lambdas&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lambda Expression Syntax:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;(parameters) -&amp;gt; { body }&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>CTS Interview Preparation</title><link>https://notxkcd.github.io/sdet-prep-site/qa-vault/interview-bibles/cts-interview-prep/</link><pubDate>Sat, 31 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://notxkcd.github.io/sdet-prep-site/qa-vault/interview-bibles/cts-interview-prep/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="personal--behavioral"&gt;Personal &amp;amp; Behavioral&lt;/h2&gt;
